REMARKS:
280300Z POSITION NEAR 28.0N 120.3E.
28AUG26. TROPICAL STORM 17W (SAUDEL), LOCATED APPROXIMATELY 375
NM WEST-NORTHWEST OF KADENA AB, HAS TRACKED WESTWARD AT 14 KNOTS
OVER THE PAST SIX HOURS. ANIMATED RADAR IMAGERY INDICATES THE SYSTEM
HAS INCREASED SPEED OVER THE PAST SIX HOURS, MAKING LANDFALL OVER
THE YUHUAN PENINSULA AT 272330Z. TS 17W IS FORECAST TO CONTINUE TO
TRACK WESTWARD INTO CENTRAL CHINA UNDER THE INFLUENCE OF A
SUBTROPICAL RIDGE (STR) CENTERED TO THE NORTHWEST. INTENSITY IS
EXPECTED TO SHARPLY DECREASE AS THE SYSTEM INTERACTS WITH THE
TERRAIN, DETERIORATING THE VORTEX RAPIDLY AND DISSIPATING 17W AS A
TROPICAL CYCLONE OVER LAND BY TAU 24. THIS IS THE FINAL WARNING ON
THIS SYSTEM BY THE JOINT TYPHOON WRNCEN PEARL HARBOR HI. THE SYSTEM
WILL BE CLOSELY MONITORED FOR SIGNS OF REGENERATION. MINIMUM CENTRAL
PRESSURE AT 280000Z IS 982 MB.
FOR SIX-HOURLY UPDATES.
